# Production guardrails

Treat `main` as production. Deploy = push to GitHub Pages (root). Custom domain file: `CNAME` → `www.prodatalytics.com`.

## Forbidden without explicit request

- Hand-editing `css/main.css`
- Changing `CNAME`, DNS notes, FormSubmit endpoints / `_next` URL / `hello@prodatalytics.com`
- Changing brand tokens, primary logo in use, or legal/contact footer blocks
- Large framework migrations or inventing `app/` / React structure
- Drive-by refactors unrelated to the user’s ask

## Sync contracts

- After CSS/Tailwind class changes: run `npm run build:css` and commit `css/main.css` (Pages has no build step).
- Header / nav / footer: edit `scripts/chrome/*` and run `python3 scripts/sync-chrome.py`. Floating contact shell is per-page.
- `pages/homepage.html` is a redirect stub; homepage content lives only in `index.html`.

## Pre-ship checklist

0. `npm run check` passes
1. Local HTTP server smoke test (not `file://`)
2. Nav, mobile menu, and assets load (no 404s)
3. Forms/FAQ still work on contact if touched
4. No accidental brand or domain regressions

See `AGENTS.md` for full Always / Ask first / Never boundaries and known hazards — ask before “fixing” them silently.
